---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Base
  title="Weekly Pool Cleaning Service | Georgetown, Round Rock, Cedar Park"
  description="Weekly pool cleaning from a factory-authorized repair crew — chemistry, brushing, baskets, and equipment checks, every visit. Call (512) 764-9867."
>
  <h1>Weekly pool cleaning service — {SITE.serviceArea}</h1>

  <p>
    Get your pool cleaned, balanced, and checked every week without thinking about it — by the
    same crew that handles emergency pump, leak, and heater repairs. That matters more than it
    sounds: most cleaning services just clean. If something's actually wrong with your equipment,
    ours can tell you on the spot instead of pointing you toward someone else.
  </p>

  <div class="dispatch">
    <dl>
      <dt>Every visit</dt>
      <dd>Water testing, chemical balancing, brushing, baskets, and a filter check</dd>
      <dt>First visit</dt>
      <dd>A straight price for your pool — no guessing over the phone</dd>
      <dt>Area</dt>
      <dd>{SITE.serviceArea}</dd>
    </dl>
    <a class="call-btn" href={SITE.phoneHref}>Call to get on the schedule</a>
    <p class="call-sub">{SITE.hoursLine}</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What's included in every visit</h2>
  <ul class="link-grid">
    <li>
      Water testing &amp; chemical balancing
      <small>Chlorine, pH, and alkalinity checked and corrected every time</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      Brushing walls, steps, and tile line
      <small>Where algae gets a foothold that skimming alone never reaches</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      Vacuuming and skimming
      <small>Floor and surface debris cleared before it has time to settle</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      Skimmer &amp; pump basket emptied
      <small>Keeps flow strong between visits</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      Filter pressure check
      <small>Caught early, before it turns into a circulation problem</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      Equipment pad visual check
      <small>Pump, filter, and heater looked over every visit, not just when something breaks</small>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why a repair company runs your weekly cleaning</h2>
  <p>
    A standard pool cleaner can tell you the water looks fine. A tech who's also{' '}
    <a href="/pool-pump-repair/">factory-authorized to repair pumps</a>, heaters, and equipment can
    tell you the pump is drawing high current, or the filter pressure is climbing faster than it
    should, weeks before either becomes a breakdown. {SITE.backing} That authorized-dealer backing
    is the same one behind every repair call we run — your weekly technician isn't guessing about
    equipment, they're trained on it.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      Call {SITE.phoneDisplay} and tell us about your pool — size, current condition, and
      anything about the equipment that's been bothering you.
    </li>
    <li>
      First visit is a full assessment: water test, equipment look-over, and a straight price for
      ongoing weekly service based on your specific pool. See our{' '}
      <a href="/guides/pool-cleaning-cost-central-texas/">pool cleaning cost guide</a> for what
      moves that number.
    </li>
    <li>
      We set a weekly day that works with your schedule and get you on the route.
    </li>
    <li>
      Every week after that: cleaned, balanced water and an equipment check, with any concerns
      flagged the same visit — not after they've become a repair call.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Already have a green pool?</h2>
  <p>
    Weekly service assumes a pool that's already in decent shape. If yours has gone green or been
    neglected for a while, that's a different starting point — see our{' '}
    <a href="/green-pool-cleanup/">green pool cleanup page</a> for an emergency recovery, then move
    to weekly service once it's clear. Many of our weekly customers started exactly that way.
  </p>

  <section class="faq">
    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <h3>Do I need to be home for the visit?</h3>
    <p>
      No — as long as our technician can reach the pool and equipment pad (through a gate code,
      side access, or similar), the visit happens on schedule whether you're home or not.
    </p>
    <h3>Do you bring the chemicals, or do I need to supply them?</h3>
    <p>
      Chemicals used during your weekly visit are part of the service — you don't need to keep a
      supply on hand or guess at dosing yourself.
    </p>
    <h3>Can I pause service, like for a vacation or the off-season?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes — let us know ahead of time and we'll adjust the schedule. Central Texas winters often
      make sense to space out anyway; see our{' '}
      <a href="/guides/how-often-should-pool-be-cleaned-texas/">
        guide on cleaning frequency by season
      </a>.
    </p>
    <h3>What happens if you find something wrong with my equipment?</h3>
    <p>
      You'll hear about it the same visit, with a straight quote before any repair work starts —
      {SITE.feeLine.toLowerCase()}
    </p>
    <h3>How is this different from your emergency green pool cleanup?</h3>
    <p>
      Weekly service is ongoing preventative care for a pool that's already in good shape.{' '}
      <a href="/green-pool-cleanup/">Green pool cleanup</a> is a one-time rescue for a pool that's
      already turned green or been neglected. Plenty of customers use one to get clear, then
      switch to the other to stay that way.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="dispatch">
    <dl>
      <dt>Every visit</dt>
      <dd>Water testing, chemical balancing, brushing, baskets, and a filter check</dd>
      <dt>First visit</dt>
      <dd>A straight price for your pool — no guessing over the phone</dd>
      <dt>Area</dt>
      <dd>{SITE.serviceArea}</dd>
    </dl>
    <a class="call-btn" href={SITE.phoneHref}>Call to get on the schedule</a>
    <p class="call-sub">{SITE.hoursLine}</p>
  </div>
</Base>
